  "report_period": "Week 25 (13th Jun to 20th Jun 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Partagas\" 173/2004 SWS, China (SS 09/2027, DD 09/2025, Scrubber fitted) of TMS Dry was committed to undisclosed interests at excess USD 13,5 mill, while the three-years-younger \"Cape Veni\" 173/2007 Bohai, China (SS 07/2027, DD 07/2025) of Olympia Ocean Carriers was committed to Chinese interests at USD 17 mill. Nissen Kaiun have committed the Mini Cape \"Baby Cassiopeia\" 110/2012 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026, Scrubber fitted) to Vietnamese interests at USD 19 mill. Remind you that earlier this month, the one-year-older \"Bastions\" 119/2011 Sanoyas, Japan (SS/DD 01/2026, Scrubber fitted) was sold at region USD 16,5 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Bright Pegasus\" 82/2013 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 04/2028, DD 06/2026, Scrubber fitted) of Meiji Shipping was committed to Middle Eastern interests at low USD 17 mill. Note that the two-years-older sister vessel \"ASL Venus\" 82/2011 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS/DD 01/2026) was sold a week ago at USD 14,4 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"FLC Celebration\" 57/2011 Qingshan, China (SS/DD 01/2026) was committed to undisclosed interests at low USD 11 mill. For comparison, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"NZ Hangzhou\" 56/2012 Qingshan, China (SS 06/2027, DD 09/2025) was sold a month ago at USD 12 mill. The Handysize \"NY Trader III\" 39/2016 Jiangmen, China (SS/DD 09/2026) of Seafarers Shipping was committed to European interests at region USD 17 mill. Note that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Western Miami\" 39/2015 Jiangmen, China (SS/DD 07/2025) was sold back in May at USD 14,5 mill. In addition, Oskar Wehr committed their \"Birte Selmer\" 35/2011 Samjin, China (SS/DD 06/2026) to clients of Nautilus Management at very high USD 9 mill. Remind you that back in March, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Atlantic Ocean\" 36/2010 Samjin, China (SS/DD 10/2025) was sold at USD 9,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Suezmax \"Nordic Thunder\" 157/2017 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 06/2027) was committed to clients of Delta Tankers at region USD 65 mill. For reference, the one-year-older \"Diamondway\" & \"Goldway\" 154/2016 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 06/2026 & SS/DD 09/2026, Scrubber fitted) were sold back in February at USD 68 mill each. Ya Sa Shipping have committed their Aframax \"Yasa Golden Marmara\" 110/2008 Mitsui, Japan (SS 07/2027, DD 08/2025) at region USD 31 mill, while the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Mare Nostrum\" 110/2009 Mitsui, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 06/2026) was sold in April at USD 34,4 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid-high usd 9,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 11,000/13,000 pd range. South East Asian trips via South America into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips via South Africa into India were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via North Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. South American trips into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/700K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 11,000 pd for 6/8 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Panamax was fixed on a period at the usd 11,500 pd basis delivery South East Asia for 5/7 months employment with redelivery AG-Japan range.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Trips from China into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips via Arabian Gulf into Australia were reported at the level of usd 9,000/10,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 150K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "South Asian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 8,000/10,000 pd. West Coast Indian trips into Continent were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. US Gulf coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were fixed around usd 17,000/18,000 pd. South American trips into Continent-mediterranean range were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
